Package: BINTS
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Breeding Bird and Insect Time Series Modelling 
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person(
      given = "Kwaku Peprah",
      family = "Adjei",
      email = "kwaku.adjei@nina.no",
      role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
Description: Provides tools for constructing and fitting Bayesian models of
    insect biomass and diversity using NIMBLE. Supports normal and lognormal
    biomass likelihoods, and normal, Poisson, and negative binomial diversity
    likelihoods. Includes continuous covariates, categorical random effects,
    year, locality, and replicate effects, linear and cubic cyclic temporal
    effects, and spatial effects based on geographic coordinates or spatial
    autocorrelation. Provides functions for preparing model data and
    constants, generating initial values, constructing cyclic spline bases
    and penalty matrices, and running Markov chain Monte Carlo estimation
    with optional Widely Applicable Information Criterion calculation.
